KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ pack expanded: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [temp.alias]/2, [temp.variadic]/5: holder_of<int &, long &> is
holder<char, int &, long &>.  When the pack of the function template using
the alias has the alias's pack's name (A), the expansion of
`typename id<A>::type...' repeats the first element: deduction forms
holder<char, int &, int &>, the instantiation of last_size's declaration
then gets nil for the second element, and the conversion fails ("symbol
'holder_of<ref_signed_int,ref_signed_long_int>' already declared with
different type").  Renaming either pack, or `id_t<A>...' through another
alias template, avoids it.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and
it fails only its WRONG assertion.
